From: Romain Naour <romain.naour@gmail.com>
Date: Wed,  9 Mar 2016 01:00:18 +0100
Subject: [Buildroot] [PATCH 1/3] support: add a customized 'missing' script
Message-ID: <1457481620-9607-1-git-send-email-romain.naour@gmail.com>
List-Id: <buildroot.busybox.net>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
To: buildroot@busybox.net

Since automake v1.12b the 'missing' script return exit status of the given
program [1]. This triggers some build failure [2] [3] when one of maintainer
tools is missing on the host.

This is the case for binutils and gdb [4] which use an updated version of the
'missing' script.

So, add a slightly modified version which return 0 even if one of maintainer
tools like makeinfo is missing on the host.
This follow the idea from Arnout about a wrapper for programs that we want to
work around [5].

[1] http://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/automake.git/commit/?id=a22717dffe37f30ef2ad2c355b68c9b3b5e4b8c7
[2] http://autobuild.buildroot.org/results/244/2442e697d8a300496434fd42fcb1ee3941d13e06/
[3] http://autobuild.buildroot.net/results/dd5/dd50ed99abb2c8495def826866b184030953f90e/
[4] https://sourceware.org/git/gitweb.cgi?p=binutils-gdb.git;a=commitdiff;h=e30465112ed4c6320dd19107302057a5f7712cf2
[5] http://lists.busybox.net/pipermail/buildroot/2016-February/151277.html

